<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 2: </span>Performance comparison of different methods on <span id="S3.T2.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">YRBS</span> and <span id="S3.T2.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">NSDUH</span> datasets.</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Bi-Modal Optimization.</h4>

<div id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To align modalities, we project the graph-based user embedding into the LLM embedding space via a learnable projection head <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{z}_{u}=P_{\text{proj}}(\mathbf{h}_{u}^{\text{agg}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext>proj</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐡</mi><mi>u</mi><mtext>agg</mtext></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{z}_{u}=P_{\text{proj}}(\mathbf{h}_{u}^{\text{agg}})</annotation></semantics></math>.
We prepend this projected graph token to the textual embeddings and feed the sequence into a frozen LLM to generate an output sequence <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y=(y_{1},\ldots,y_{r})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y=(y_{1},\ldots,y_{r})</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="S3.E6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\theta,\phi}(Y|\mathcal{Z},\mathbf{z}_{u})=\prod_{i=1}^{r}p_{\theta,\phi}\!\left(y_{i}|y_{&lt;i},\,[\mathbf{z}_{u};\mathcal{Z}]\right)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>u</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>r</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\theta,\phi}(Y|\mathcal{Z},\mathbf{z}_{u})=\prod_{i=1}^{r}p_{\theta,\phi}\!\left(y_{i}|y_{&lt;i},\,[\mathbf{z}_{u};\mathcal{Z}]\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(6)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math> denotes frozen LLM parameters and <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϕ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi</annotation></semantics></math> includes trainable parameters of the graph encoder and <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{\text{proj}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext>proj</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{\text{proj}}</annotation></semantics></math>. The concatenation <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[\mathbf{z}_{u};\mathcal{Z}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[\mathbf{z}_{u};\mathcal{Z}]</annotation></semantics></math> forms the full prompt, with <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{z}_{u}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{z}_{u}</annotation></semantics></math> acting as a soft graph-conditioned prefix. In parallel, we feed <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{h}_{u}^{\text{agg}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝐡</mi><mi>u</mi><mtext>agg</mtext></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{h}_{u}^{\text{agg}}</annotation></semantics></math> to a lightweight classifier for illicit drug use prediction.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y\in\{0,1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y\in\{0,1\}</annotation></semantics></math> be the ground-truth label and <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{y}</annotation></semantics></math> the classifier output. We supervise the LLM with a verbalized label token (e.g., <span id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Yes</span>/<span id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">No</span>) at the beginning of <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y</annotation></semantics></math>. The total loss combines a generation loss and a classification loss:</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<table id="S3.EGx1" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.Ex1"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{\text{bi}}=\mathcal{L}_{\text{gen}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>bi</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>gen</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{\text{bi}}=\mathcal{L}_{\text{gen}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+\mathcal{L}_{\text{cls}},\quad\mathcal{L}_{\text{cls}}=\mathrm{CE}\big(\hat{y},y\big)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>cls</mtext></msub></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>cls</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>CE</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\mathcal{L}_{\text{cls}},\quad\mathcal{L}_{\text{cls}}=\mathrm{CE}\big(\hat{y},y\big),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.E7"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{\text{gen}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>gen</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{\text{gen}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=-\log p_{\theta,\phi}\!\left(y\mid\mathbf{z}_{u},\mathcal{Z}\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\log p_{\theta,\phi}\!\left(y\mid\mathbf{z}_{u},\mathcal{Z}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(7)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Gradients from <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\text{bi}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>bi</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\text{bi}}</annotation></semantics></math> update <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϕ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi</annotation></semantics></math> only. This dual-objective setup provides optimization signals from both textual space and graph space, enabling GNN-based structural reasoning and LLM-based textual interpretation.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Detection and Explanation.</h4>

<div id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">At inference time, we use the graph classifier for illicit drug detection, and additionally prompt the LLM to justify the decision in natural language. This output serves as a post-hoc explanation, enabling qualitative analysis and uncovering interpretable patterns associated with illicit drug use.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S4" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">4 </span>Experiments</h2>

<figure id="S4.T3" class="ltx_table">
<div id="S4.T3.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_center ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:345.0pt;height:41pt;vertical-align:-19.1pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(-138.9pt,16.5pt) scale(0.553870448631261,0.553870448631261) ;">
<table id="S4.T3.2.1" class="ltx_tabular ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
